      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Single coronary artery is a rare anomaly with or without other cardiac diseases and uncertain prognostic importance. It may be related with sudden death. We report a case of 64 years old man with single coronary artery and unstable angina, successful treated with medical therapy, for long time (six years)."},
